2.4.2.3
The time scales
The model signal pfk corresponds either to a forecast of the market price, or, to a direction
forecast of the market price observed at ﬁxed time intervals tk  k  δ, where k  1, ..., Nk is an integer and δ  ∆t
is a ﬁxed fraction of time. We will suppose that the model forecast last for the period τ  n  u, where u is a ﬁxed
unit of time (say in second) and n  1, 2, ... is an integer.
2.4.2.4
Measuring returns
We are interested in the forecast for the learner h for a ﬁxed period d. Thus, to validate
the forecast, we are interested in the kth log-return rL,dpkq  rLpk, k   dq for the d period deﬁned in Equation (9.12).
We have two time scales, the one given by the model signals and the market prices observed at tick time levels.
