4.2.3
The algorithm
The predictive model proposed by Van den Poel et al. [2016] is made of two layers, namely the Feature Engineering (selection) layer and the Prediction layer. This is similar to stacking described in Appendix (13.5). Rather than
using the Deterministic Data Preparation Layer (DDPL) proposed by Patel et al. [2015], the authors chose to combine the continuous indicators with some technical trading rules which give signals based on criteria for identifying
market entry and exit points (see Appendix (11.5.1)). The Feature Selection layer devises the trading rules for each
technical indicator. The input of the model are the return values corresponding to the dependent variable along with
the continuous-valued technical indicators (see Appendix (11.2)), single technical trading rules and complex trading
