6.4.3
Predicting trends
A simple way of using TD methods to predict ﬁnancial patterns is to follow the example on bounded random walk
given in Appendix (16.2.3). The walk is a symmetric process bounded above and below by a barrier level, bup and
bdown, respectively. The aim is to ﬁnd the conditional probability of a walk reaching a barrier level, given that it was
in each of the other states.
We assume that the market return in Equation (6.2) is composed of a deterministic drift and some noise, a random
walk. We are interested in assessing simple upward trends in market returns. We consider the sequences e deﬁned
above where the vector xt contains the standardised market return pr at time t, and the outcome z  bup is an up barrier
