represent them as tpx1, d1q, ..., pxT , dT qu with T ordered pairs. To be consistent with the articles described we keep
the P ordered pairs, and we let p  P be the most recent observation.
Refenes et al.
[1997] proposed a simple modiﬁcation to the error backpropagation procedure taking into account
gradually changing input-output pairs. The procedure is based on the principle of discounted least-squares whereby
learning is biased towards more recent observations with long term effects experiencing exponential decay through
time. The cumulative error calculated by the DLS procedure is given by
