and magnitude within the trend. Hence, to reﬂect this point when evaluating the performance of a forecasting model,
Yao et al. [1996] used the correctness of trend and a paper proﬁt. They proposed a proﬁt based adjusted weight factor
for backpropagation network training by adding a factor containing proﬁt, direction, and time information to the error
function.
9.4.3
Time dependent direction proﬁt
In order to take proﬁt gain into account, Caldwell [1995] proposed a weighted directional symmetry (WDS) function
which penalise more heavily the incorrectly predicted directions than the correct ones. The cumulative error function
