10.2.2.1
Discrete Wavelet Transform
DWT is the most basic wavelet decomposition, Figure (20) shows how it
can be done. H, L and H’, L’ respectively stands for high-pass, low-pass ﬁlters for wavelet decomposition and reconstitution. In the decomposition phase, L and H remove respectively the higher frequencies and the lower frequencies
to give an approximation and a detail of signal x. The result is then downsampled by 2. The right part of the ﬁgure
denotes the reserve process and is known as the reconstruction phase.
