Ensemble models
We brieﬂy introduce ensemble models. More details can be found in textbooks by Rokach [2010], Zhou [2012],
among others.
We let X and Y be the input and output spaces, D the probability distribution, D the data set (sample), H the set of
hypotheses, Ipq the indicator function. We let x be an instance or feature vector. For example, we consider the training
data set D  tpx1, y1q, ..., pxm, ymqu where the instances xi are independent and identically distributed (i.i.d.) and
yi  fpxiq where f is the ground-truth target function. That is, xi is a vector and yi takes value in R. The learning
process aim at constructing a learner h minimising the generalisation error
