14.3
Deﬁning multifractality
Multifractality or anomalous scaling allows for a richer variation of the behaviour of a process across different scales.
Equation (14.58) shows that this variability of scaling laws can be translated into the variability of the Hurst index,
which is no-longer constant. Following Abry et al. [2002] and Wendt [2008] who both gave a synthetic overview of
the concepts of scale invariance, scaling analysis, and multifractal analysis, we are going to introduce multifractality.
