large frequencies, νM Ñ 8 (small scales), deﬁne long-range dependent processes and monofractal processes. Scale
invariance is generally deﬁned as the power law behaviours of (the time average of the qth power of) multiresolution
quantities, denoted TXpa, tq with respect to the analysis scale a, for a given (large) range of scales a P pam, aMq,
