original error function Epwq. This training rule is known as the Widrow-Hoff rule (see Widrow et al. [1960]), or the
delta rule, or sometimes the least-mean-square (LMS) rule. Widrow et al. devised the ADALINE (Adaptive Linear
Neuron or later Adaptive Linear Element), which is the name of a physical device that implemented a single layer
artiﬁcial neural network. In the learning phase, the weights are adjusted according to the weighted sum of the inputs.
The difference
